# ADR 0023 · NATIVE-AGENTS.md §6.2 · UX-SPEC §3.1 — a new user hands work to an agent and answers
# its approval with the pointer alone; the only keyboard input is the prompt typed into the
# composer the click focused.
#
# Double-click the worktree → the strip's `+` → Codex thread (menu item 2: Terminal, Claude
# thread, Codex thread, …) → click the composer, type, Send → `← Worktrees` while the agent works
# → the title bar's needs-you pill goes to the one waiting thread → Allow once. The `agents`
# preset gives Codex `edit-approval.json`, whose one file change stops at a permission gate. The
# gate is held for twenty seconds (TESTING-HARNESS §5), which is the budget from its appearance
# to the click that answers it.
#
# Virtual-lane only: it takes shots.
fixture: agents
await idle 30000
assert screen == Hub && overlay absent && targets["titlebar.needs_you"] absent

# A double-click opens the worktree, as ⏎ does.
click left 2 worktrees.row[0]
await screen == Workspace 20000
await targets["tabs.new"] exists 20000

# `+` → Codex thread starts a thread in a new tab, selected, its composer taking the keyboard.
click tabs.new
await targets["menu.item[2]"] exists 5000
shot new-tab-menu
click menu.item[2]
await agents.threads[0].provider == codex 20000
await lists.tabs.selected.badges[0] == codex 20000
await focused == agents.composer 20000
await idle 30000
click agents.composer
type apply the README fix
click agents.send
await agents.threads[0].state != idle 30000

# Back to the Hub while it works: the gate reaches the title bar's needs-you pill.
click workspace.back
await screen == Hub 10000
await agents.threads[0].pending_gate == permission 30000
await targets["titlebar.needs_you"] exists 10000
assert agents.threads[0].state == needs_you
shot needs-you

# One thread waiting: the pill opens it, with its approval dock up.
click titlebar.needs_you
await screen == Workspace 20000
await mode == Agent 10000
await targets["agents.approval.allow_once"] exists 10000
assert agents.threads[0].pending_gate == permission && overlay absent
shot approval

# Allow once, by its button: the gate closes and the turn finishes on its own.
click agents.approval.allow_once
await agents.threads[0].pending_gate absent 30000
assert agents.threads[0].state != needs_you
await agents.threads[0].state == idle 30000
assert sticky_error absent && targets["titlebar.needs_you"] absent
dump allowed
quit
